#section[M. Mathematics in context][Each case below puts mathematics where a reader meets it.]

#case("M-01", "Inline maths mid-sentence")[
The energy $E = m c^2$ follows from the rest mass alone.
]

#case("M-02", "Inline fraction")[
The ratio $a/b$ equals $frac(1, 2)$ when $b = 2a$.
]

#case("M-03", "Numbered display equation")[
#set math.equation(numbering: "(1)")
Newton gives the law
$ F = m a $
which we use throughout.
]

#case("M-04", "Display with a limit and fraction")[
The velocity is
$ v = lim_(Delta t -> 0) (Delta p)/(Delta t) $
which is the derivative of position.
]

#case("M-05", "Matrix")[
The rotation matrix is
$ R = mat(cos theta, -sin theta; sin theta, cos theta) $
for an angle $theta$.
]

#case("M-06", "A sentence that is only maths")[
$x^2 + y^2 = r^2$.
]

#case("M-07", "Sum and integral displays")[
$ sum_(i=1)^n i = (n(n+1))/2 quad "and" quad integral_0^1 x^2 dif x = 1/3 $
]

#case("M-08", "Sub- and superscripts inline")[
Each term $x_i^2$ multiplies the entry $a_(i j)$ of the matrix.
]

#case("M-09", "Greek inside maths")[
We require $alpha + beta = gamma$ and $Delta x > 0$.
]

#case("M-10", "Roots, norms and absolute values")[
